  "authoringNote": "Exactly 50 slots are supplied, counted by hand: the encounter, order, receipt and supplier record (4), f26g-lineage v1 and v2 (2), the restricted f26g-restricted v1 (1, metadata only), the declared unreadable f26g-unreadable v1 (1) and 42 replicated filler notes f26g-filler-01 to f26g-filler-42 (42). Superseded, restricted, unreadable and generated slots all count; the two recipe templates, the metadata sidecars, the case, the manifest and the oracle are not documents. 50 is within the bound, so the loader accepts the fixture and the snapshot is assessed. f26g-lineage v2 supersedes v1 by trusted committed metadata of the same document ID, kind and subject (C08), so supersededDocuments is exactly [f26g-lineage v1]; v1 is valid and case-bound but contributes no fact and is named nowhere else (C07, C09). f26g-restricted v1 has accessStatus restricted, a null contentHash and no payload, so its first R09 condition is R09.access_restricted. f26g-unreadable v1 holds a hash-matching, valid note body but its accessStatus is unreadable, so its first R09 condition is R09.access_unreadable (after access_restricted and hash_mismatch, which do not hold). Both are bound to the case by metadata subject only and are not quarantined. R09 is restricted for the authorization coordinator, the first outcome with a held condition; the unreadable condition keeps its own unreadable routing to the coordinator and needs_information. R09 affectedDocuments is the union of its condition documents, [f26g-restricted v1, f26g-unreadable v1] (C07). R02 passes: every current usable note states the case beneficiary name and identifier exactly, so R02 cites the encounter, order and receipt pairs (6), the f26g-lineage v2 pair (2) and the 42 filler pairs (84), 92 in all; the superseded, restricted and unreadable notes contribute no citation (C05). Note titles and texts map to no evidence field, so the notes add no clinical fact. The receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order, so R05 passes citing four facts. R04 passes citing six facts. No note is an order, encounter, receipt or supplier record, so no R01 or R03 to R05 candidate arises. The rest follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and the final signed order (2026-09-04) both name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001; the order is after the encounter, on a different date, and within the inclusive C01 bound 2027-02-26; the order item code K0823 equals the case; the named supplier record f26g-supplier-status v1 is usable and states non_exempt, established, no new enrollment, no ownership change and the interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31, which contains the assessment date 2026-10-18. R01 passes citing the seven supplier record facts and the order item code; R03 passes citing the nine order facts. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false (the null evaluation date supplies no fact); no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 passes on the reviewed pack and the supported date. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. The state is needs_information from R09 alone. Quarantine is empty, and the parent affectedDocuments of every rule except R09 is empty.",
